{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PASS-1 plan-review (G7 leaf-parent containment) note — informational, cross-referenced from the G7 eval fixture `G7-R-out-of-parent-scope` (src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-g7.eval.yaml).\n\nThe fixture models a HYPOTHETICAL leaf that both (a) derives the code-review block threshold AND (b) flips the `security` criterion to blocking in criteria_routing.json under a parent whose plan is only \"derive the threshold + commit the derivation script/artifact.\" That hypothetical leaf is a G7 fire: the blocking flip is out-of-parent-scope work the parent leaves to a sibling.\n\nFor grounding: this ticket (b9c0) is the REAL sibling that legitimately owns the `security` blocking flip, and the real derivation story 9f25 explicitly scopes \"NO routing/config change here (that is the sibling enablement story).\" So the correct decomposition (9f25 derives; b9c0 flips) is exactly the boundary the fixture's bad leaf violates. No action required on b9c0 — this comment only records the cross-reference."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785711183991338001,"uuid":"231054cc-115c-4e52-96f6-d93f8241d7ea"}